03:38:52,890 --> 03:38:54,570
I don't know if I'd enjoy Lunaset.

3656
03:38:54,650 --> 03:38:55,350
I don't know what it is.

3657
03:38:55,530 --> 03:38:56,350
But I think it's on my list.

3658
03:38:56,570 --> 03:38:57,630
I recognize the name.

3659
03:38:58,810 --> 03:38:59,810
Yeah, it's on the list.

3660
03:39:03,490 --> 03:39:06,030
I hate that Sony's trying to get rid of physical game copies.

3661
03:39:06,310 --> 03:39:07,250
Honest, I don't even care.

3662
03:39:07,570 --> 03:39:08,470
I gotta be honest.

3663
03:39:09,770 --> 03:39:10,490
It's inevitable.

3664
03:39:10,870 --> 03:39:13,590
I mean, we live in a world where everything is digital nowadays.

3665
03:39:13,750 --> 03:39:14,570
Are you really surprised?

3666
03:39:15,550 --> 03:39:16,090
I'm not.

3667
03:39:16,970 --> 03:39:18,890
I'm surprised it's happening this late.

3668
03:39:22,760 --> 03:39:23,200
Interesting.

3669
03:39:23,420 --> 03:39:26,160
You rated Silksong higher than the Hollow Knight before the statistical thing.

3670
03:39:26,220 --> 03:39:26,900
Now it's the opposite.

3671
03:39:27,040 --> 03:39:27,640
That's the thing.

3672
03:39:27,760 --> 03:39:29,180
That's so interesting about this Dawn.

3673
03:39:31,560 --> 03:39:34,040
This one is much more truthful.

3674
03:39:34,660 --> 03:39:39,280
And I think it has something to do with the fact that I had just finished Silksong, you know?

3675
03:39:39,640 --> 03:39:41,140
So I had recency bias.

3676
03:39:41,340 --> 03:39:42,160
Which is a big thing.

3677
03:39:43,100 --> 03:39:46,260
But when you're doing this, you can't really lie to the system, you know?

3678
03:39:47,500 --> 03:39:48,720
So it's gonna count...

3679
03:39:48,720 --> 03:39:50,500
Like, it's more truthful than I can ever be.

3680
03:39:51,840 --> 03:39:54,720
If you tell someone or ask someone to make a...

3681
03:39:55,140 --> 03:40:00,360
a list of their favorite games and rank everything, you know, from a 1 to a 100, absolutely.

3682
03:40:01,200 --> 03:40:03,620
That is almost impossible to do.

3683
03:40:04,440 --> 03:40:13,140
Because you keep saying to yourself, Oh, but wait, if this guy is at 83 and the other guy was at 82, but I like the 82 more, so I gotta move that up and then it's a mess.

3684
03:40:13,600 --> 03:40:14,540
It's a real mess.

3685
03:40:15,780 --> 03:40:19,100
There's a lot of surprises in that list now, now that I did the comparisons.

3686
03:40:19,600 --> 03:40:25,000
Some games that I rated a lot higher, probably because of recency bias, are now much lower.

3687
03:40:26,300 --> 03:40:29,740
The cool thing is, though, I have timestamps for all these comparisons.

3688
03:40:30,380 --> 03:40:41,680
So over time, when I do more and more and more, also as new games get added, I can make, like, some kind of graph or comparison of how my taste or preferences change over time.

3689
03:40:42,240 --> 03:40:44,840
You know, that could be some interesting data angle there.

3690
03:40:45,640 --> 03:40:47,320
I store all kinds of information.

3691
03:40:47,540 --> 03:40:53,500
I even store response time and which ones I pick, left or right, and how often, and stuff like that, you know.

3692
03:40:54,300 --> 03:40:55,300
Could be kind of fun.

3693
03:40:59,070 --> 03:41:01,010
What if you voted right after finishing the game?

3694
03:41:01,150 --> 03:41:02,850
Wouldn't that still be affected by recency bias?

3695
03:41:03,010 --> 03:41:03,370
It would!

3696
03:41:03,730 --> 03:41:06,770
And that's why someone else mentioned this on the Discord, actually.

3697
03:41:07,210 --> 03:41:15,710
And I think what I'm gonna do is that when I finish a game, I'm not going to vote it or enter it into the voting until I have finished the next game.

3698
03:41:15,710 --> 03:41:19,250
So the game I'm incorporating is always one game behind.

3699
03:41:20,990 --> 03:41:22,610
Because recency bias is real.

3700
03:41:24,290 --> 03:41:30,070
And there's also, you know, rose-tinted glasses about older games, and I'm definitely guilty of that.

3701
03:41:30,450 --> 03:41:34,250
You know, when I did the comparisons, I was looking at Spyro, you know?

3702
03:41:34,410 --> 03:41:35,390
Like, that's one of the comparisons.

3703
03:41:35,530 --> 03:41:37,470
I'm like, damn, I had so much fun with that as a kid.

3704
03:41:37,910 --> 03:41:40,870
But if I played it now, I don't know if I would like it as much.

3705
03:41:41,450 --> 03:41:44,130
I'm basing that off my memory of how much I liked it, right?

3706
03:41:46,510 --> 03:41:47,810
Yeah, Ducky Bird, exactly.

3707
03:41:49,910 --> 03:41:52,010
Isaac is not getting rated anytime soon.

3708
03:41:52,910 --> 03:41:54,750
I mean, Isaac is...

3709
03:41:55,790 --> 03:41:56,830
It's a good game, man.

3710
03:41:57,490 --> 03:42:00,650
I was about to give it a rating, but then I remembered, don't do that.

3711
03:42:00,790 --> 03:42:02,810
Let the system decide that for you.

3712
03:42:06,630 --> 03:42:09,010
How much time did you get when you were doing your comparisons?

3713
03:42:09,870 --> 03:42:10,510
Infinite time.

3714
03:42:10,690 --> 03:42:11,890
I didn't put a timer on myself.

3715
03:42:12,510 --> 03:42:14,310
It did record the response time, though.

3716
03:42:14,470 --> 03:42:15,370
Like, that data is there.

3717
03:42:16,730 --> 03:42:18,930
But I didn't actually put a timer on it.

3718
03:42:25,820 --> 03:42:28,280
I'm just playing with the idea of putting the timer there for you guys.

3719
03:42:28,400 --> 03:42:29,160
Maybe I won't do it.

3720
03:42:30,060 --> 03:42:31,660
Maybe I'll have it as, like, an option.

3721
03:42:31,820 --> 03:42:33,780
No, no, because it needs to be the same for everyone.

3722
03:42:34,500 --> 03:42:35,180
Yeah, I don't know yet.

3723
03:42:40,960 --> 03:42:46,160
How much would you guys hate if you had to make an account to do the voting on the website?

3724
03:42:47,080 --> 03:42:51,720
Because that is one way to do, like, a capture and make sure there's no bots or something like that.

3725
03:42:54,000 --> 03:42:54,420
Because...

3726
03:42:54,420 --> 03:42:58,020
I would probably be a little annoyed having to make an account.

3727
03:43:01,300 --> 03:43:02,860
So I totally get that, you know?

3728
03:43:04,240 --> 03:43:09,820
It would be better in the long run, but it's also, like, a friction to get people to vote.

3729
03:43:09,820 --> 03:43:12,960
It's much easier to just give a link and they can instantly start voting, right?

3730
03:43:20,360 --> 03:43:23,260
Not to be that guy, but I would love for you to give Terraria another chance.

3731
03:43:26,180 --> 03:43:30,300
Maybe if there's, like, an update 4.0, I'll check it out.

3732
03:43:30,320 --> 03:43:32,960
But honestly, I just don't really like that game very much.

3733
03:43:34,180 --> 03:43:40,220
And contrary to popular belief, it had nothing to do with the difficulty that I chose.

3734
03:43:42,300 --> 03:43:44,920
I have many qualms with that game.

3735
03:43:47,160 --> 03:43:48,680
I love making accounts.

3736
03:43:49,080 --> 03:43:50,640
Nobody loves making accounts.

3737
03:43:51,460 --> 03:43:52,820
Like, one of the worst things ever.

3738
03:43:55,950 --> 03:43:57,470
I could auth with Twitch.

3739
03:43:58,230 --> 03:43:59,610
But it's still...

3740
03:44:00,310 --> 03:44:02,190
The whole idea of making an account.

3741
03:44:09,380 --> 03:44:10,180
Yeah, we'll see.

3742
03:44:10,360 --> 03:44:11,040
I, uh...

3743
03:44:11,040 --> 03:44:13,260
Maybe I'll store all your data, you know?

3744
03:44:13,500 --> 03:44:20,220
Maybe I'll store your device and your operating system, your browser, everything, so I can fingerprint you and make sure you can't cheat.

3745
03:44:21,840 --> 03:44:24,560
I think that's actually against some EU laws.

3746
03:44:24,980 --> 03:44:26,840
So I technically can't do that, I think.

3747
03:44:27,980 --> 03:44:28,960
I'm not gonna do that.

3748
03:44:34,320 --> 03:44:36,920
But I'll definitely make some kind of, uh...

3749
03:44:36,920 --> 03:44:38,280
Cloudflare thing, I think.

3750
03:44:38,620 --> 03:44:41,840
Some invisible Cloudflare turnstile...

3751
03:44:41,840 --> 03:44:42,320
Something.

3752
03:44:44,500 --> 03:44:45,660
Because that's an easy win.

3753
03:44:49,020 --> 03:44:50,660
Have to give a blood sample to a vote.

3754
03:44:50,720 --> 03:44:51,300
I like that!

3755
03:44:51,700 --> 03:44:54,660
Or you have to mail in your votes to a physical address.

3756
03:44:55,040 --> 03:44:55,860
What do you think of that?

3757
03:44:58,840 --> 03:44:59,720
Alright, I'm out of here.

3758
03:45:00,060 --> 03:45:00,880
Thanks for watching, guys.

3759
03:45:01,120 --> 03:45:01,800
This was great.

3760
03:45:02,120 --> 03:45:04,060
Another unbeaten run.

3761
03:45:04,060 --> 03:45:05,440
At least in terms of the streaks.

3762
03:45:06,200 --> 03:45:08,280
I'll see you in the next stream slash video.

3763
03:45:08,460 --> 03:45:08,660
Bye-bye.
